{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1116847-making-my-own-setting-yay-or-nay","id":1116847,"title":"Making my own setting: yay or nay?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-16T08:40:24-07:00","id":1116847,"title":"Making my own setting: yay or nay?","content":"Hi folks. Just like ever player in the whole universe, I, too, am creating my own setting. Well, I did a few impro sessions about 15 years ago and it was much fun. It was about the player characters embodying the power of demons hunting for corrupted souls. It was about a secret war of sins and monolithical strict angels with a god complex. Yeah - you can see now what we think is fun. XD<br /> <br /> The working title is &quot;Demonic Lands&quot;. Yep - not very creative. I know.<br /> <br /> My gaming group and I still think about those games from time to time even though we had no more than maybe three sessions more than a decade ago. But even after so many years the game is still unfinished and barely formalised. Now I want to change that, probably with nWoD as the basic rules set. Sadly, my job will take a lot of time from me for the next three months so I will make little progress. That should change at this year's end. If you are interested, I might post here that little progress that I make from time to time. Well, I will likely post most of the progress anyway ;-)<br /> <br /> I am not a great illustrator, but I have basic drawing skills so I made some illustrations which I'd like to share with you for the start:<br /> <a href=\"http://www.lustigesrollenspiel.de/diverses/Clipboard.gif\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.lustigesrollenspiel.de/di.../Clipboard.gif</a><br /> <br /> Maybe this will help you get an impression of what this game is about. The pics contain the sins, the incarnations of demons, some enemies and a map of hell. Everything is still quite basic. Ah - and I am not a native English speaker, so please look kindly upon my errors.<br /> <br /> I'd love to hear any feedback, impressions and ideas as time goes by. Is this something to share or would I better file that as a heartbreaker and keep it locked, ending this thread? Really: be honest! If this seems to be boring to you, just say so. I am German and I appreciate frank and open criticism (about my work - not about my person).<br /> <br /> Thanks for your interest.<br /> Dailor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1138-dailor","user":"dailor","date":". 07-16-2017, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1138-dailor","name":"dailor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T19:57:45-07:00","id":1117063,"title":"","content":"The art is fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I really like the broad stroke impressions of them in bold simple colors. <br /> <br /> The fact that you have embraced a story and setting and world for over ten years speaks to the passion and connection you feel to it. I've been a WoD player for maybe eight years now? I also embrace stories and characters that are no longer in play. Personally I think these forums need more of that &quot;I really play&quot; sharing to inspire others who might otherwise think like you - that others will find their stories dull. <br /> <br /> I suppose some people will, other people will not. Throw your thoughts out at us and let's see!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":